<div class="article-detail-page">
    <div class="article-body">

        <p>Cloning lets you add listings from one show to another without creating separate listings. Cloned items share the same inventory, so when an item sells out in one show, it also appears sold out in any other shows you've cloned it to.</p>
        <p>You can clone eligible listings from past or upcoming shows in the iOS app or on Lively.africa. Cloning isn't currently available on Android.</p>

        <p><strong>On this page:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="#how-clone">How to clone listings</a></li>
            <li><a href="#know-cloning">What to know about cloning</a></li>
            <li><a href="#cloning-vs-duplicating">Cloning vs. duplicating</a></li>
        </ul>

        <hr />

        <h2 id="how-clone">How to clone listings</h2>

        <p>You can only clone items to upcoming shows that have already been scheduled.</p>

        <div class="article-tabs">
            <div class="article-tabs__nav">
                <button class="article-tabs__tab is-active" type="button">In the app (iOS only)</button>
                <button class="article-tabs__tab" type="button">From Lively.africa</button>
            </div>

            <div class="article-tabs__panel is-active">
                @* GAP: the iOS app tab steps were not captured in the PDF screenshots (only the Lively.africa steps were visible). Reconstructed to mirror the web flow - verify against the live page. *@
                <ol>
                    <li>Go to your Shows in Seller Hub.</li>
                    <li>Find the show you want to clone items from.</li>
                    <li>Tap <strong>View and clone items from this show</strong>.</li>
                    <li>Use the dropdown to select the upcoming show you want to add the items to.</li>
                    <li>Check the box next to each listing you want to clone, or check <strong>Select All</strong>.</li>
                    <li>Tap <strong>Clone</strong>.</li>
                </ol>
            </div>

            <div class="article-tabs__panel">
                <ol>
                    <li>Go to your Shows in Seller Hub.</li>
                    <li>Find the show you want to clone items from.</li>
                    <li>Click <strong>View and clone items from this show</strong>.</li>
                    <li>Use the dropdown to select the upcoming show you want to add the items to.</li>
                    <li>Check the box next to each listing you want to clone, or check <strong>Select All</strong>.</li>
                    <li>Click <strong>Clone</strong>.</li>
                </ol>
            </div>
        </div>

        <h2 id="know-cloning">What to know about cloning</h2>

        <ul>
            <li><strong>Cloned items share inventory.</strong> Cloning does not create additional stock. For example, if you have one item and clone it into two upcoming shows, selling it in one show will make it sold out in the other.</li>
            <li><strong>Only certain listings can be cloned.</strong> You can clone unsold Auction and Buy It Now listings from past or upcoming shows.</li>
            <li><strong>Changes apply everywhere the item is cloned.</strong> If you edit a cloned item, your changes apply anywhere that item has been cloned.</li>
            <li><strong>Temporary Listings can not be cloned.</strong> They are designed to disappear once your show ends.</li>
            <li><strong>Marketplace listings can not be cloned into a show.</strong> To add one to a show, open the listing, select <strong>Options</strong>, then <strong>Assign to a Live Show</strong>.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="cloning-vs-duplicating">Cloning vs. duplicating</h2>

        <p>Cloning and duplicating work differently:</p>

        <ul>
            <li><strong>Cloning</strong> lets you use the same listing and inventory across multiple shows.</li>
            <li><strong>Duplicating</strong> creates a separate listing with its own inventory.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>If you want to create a separate copy of a listing, you can duplicate it from <strong>Seller Hub</strong> then <a href="#">Inventory</a>.</p>

